    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d65">

                <pb facs="d65-01" n="1" xml:id="d65-01"/>

                <head>65. Memorandum From the President’s Deputy Assistant for National Security
                    Affairs (Scowcroft) to the Executive Secretary of the Department of State
                        (Pickering)<anchor n="1" xml:id="d65-f1"/>
                    <anchor n="2" xml:id="d65-f2"/>
                </head>
                <dateline>
                    <placeName>Washington</placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian" when="1974-01-29"
                        >January 29, 1974</date>
                </dateline>
                <p>The President has authorized the Department of State to begin the normalization
                    of relations with Burundi. This normalization should commence with modest
                    allocation of resources in areas such as self-help assistance, population
                    projects, and cultural exchanges, and it should be understood that these steps
                    are predicated on continued evidence that the Government of Burundi is following
                    a national policy of respect for human rights.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed> Brent Scowcroft </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d65-f1" n="1" type="source" xml:id="d65-f1-content">
                <p>Source: National Archives, Nixon Presidential Materials, NSC Files, Box 735,
                    Country Files, Africa, Burundi. Secret.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d65-f2" n="2" xml:id="d65-f2-content">
                <p> Scowcroft notified Pickering that the President had authorized the Department to
                    begin the normalization of relations with Burundi.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
